2
00:08:24,000 --> 00:08:30,000
The Second Arrival is a science fiction, horror film directed by Kevin Tenney.

3
00:12:36,000 --> 00:12:42,000
After Zane Ziminski is found dead five people received
envelopes with details of an alien invasion.

4
00:16:48,000 --> 00:16:54,000
This group of five includes 3 scientists, Zane's brother Jack, and a reporter.

5
00:21:00,000 --> 00:21:06,000
Quickly, the group is down to three and then Jack and Bridget, the reporter.

6
00:25:12,000 --> 00:25:18,000
With a small piece of alien technology, they must escape from the aliens, who
take human form, and try to convince others that aliens exist.

7
00:29:24,000 --> 00:29:30,000
Jack Addison, played by Patrick Muldoon.

8
00:33:36,000 --> 00:33:42,000
Bridget Riordan, played by Jane Sibbett.

9
00:37:48,000 --> 00:37:54,000
Prof. Nelson Zarcoff, played by Michael Sarrazin.

10
00:42:00,000 --> 00:42:06,000
Sandra Wolf, played by Catherine Blythe.

11
00:46:12,000 --> 00:46:18,000
Wolan, played by Michael Scherer.

12
00:50:24,000 --> 00:50:30,000
Burke, played by Larry Day.

13
00:54:36,000 --> 00:54:42,000
Arrival is a 2016 American science fiction drama film directed by Denis Villeneuve and written
by Eric Heisserer, based on the 1998 novella "Story of Your Life" by Ted Chiang.

14
00:58:48,000 --> 00:58:54,000
The film stars Amy Adams as Louise Banks, a linguist enlisted by the United States Army to discover how to
communicate with extraterrestrials who have arrived on Earth, before tensions lead to war.

15
01:03:00,000 --> 01:03:06,000
Jeremy Renner, Forest Whitaker, and Michael
Stuhlbarg appear in supporting roles.

16
01:07:12,000 --> 01:07:18,000
Arrival had its world premiere at the Venice Film Festival on September 1, 2016, and was
released theatrically in the United States by Paramount Pictures on November 11, 2016.

17
01:11:24,000 --> 01:11:30,000
It grossed $203 million worldwide and was widely praised, particularly for Adams's performance,
Villeneuve's direction, and the exploration of communication with extraterrestrial intelligence.

18
01:15:36,000 --> 01:15:42,000
Considered one of the best films of 2016, Arrival appeared on numerous critics' year-end lists and
was selected by the American Film Institute as one of ten "Movies of the Year".

19
01:19:48,000 --> 01:19:54,000
It received eight nominations at the 89th Academy Awards, including Best Picture, Best
Director, Best Cinematography, Best Adapted Screenplay, and won Best Sound Editing.

20
01:24:00,000 --> 01:24:06,000
For her performance, Adams received nominations for a BAFTA, SAG, Critics' Choice; at the 74th Golden Globe Awards, Adams was nominated for
the Golden Globe Award for Best Actress and Jóhann Jóhannsson was nominated for the Golden Globe Award for Best Original Score.

21
01:28:12,000 --> 01:28:18,000
The film was awarded the Ray Bradbury Award for Outstanding Dramatic
Presentation and the Hugo Award for Best Dramatic Presentation in 2017.

22
01:32:24,000 --> 01:32:30,000
The score by Jóhann was nominated for Best Score Soundtrack
for Visual Media at the 60th Grammy Awards.

23
01:36:36,000 --> 01:36:42,000
The film explores themes of extraterrestrial technology,
investigation, global warming, space invasion, sequel.

24
01:40:48,000 --> 01:40:54,000
The tone is dark and thought_provoking.
